  "read": "No new close today, so the number is still Wednesday's 21. How the holiday took the news: futures held about +0.5% all day (Investing.com) even after the FT reported Nvidia halted AI server shipments to four Southeast Asian countries; Asian chip markets rose and Europe gained. Bad news is still not pushing prices down outside single chip names, but the holiday tape is thin, so this proves less than a full session would.",
  "positioned": "Still hedged into a four-day weekend: VIX near 27-28, fear curve 1.08 (near-term protection costs more), staples up and chips down hard over the month. Wednesday's money went to cyclicals and equal-weight, not chips. Few are long semiconductors.",
  "surprise": "Caught wrong-footed if Friday's half day holds the rebound: SPY above 712.14 and through 718.43, with NVDA above 150.50 despite the halt. The other side: the halt widening, or an OPEC+ (Nov 29) or Gulf headline, sending SPY back under 703.81."
